    "# Binôme B — Convolutional Autoencoder for road anomaly detection\n",
    "\n",
    "**CRISP-DM phases:** Data Preparation (AE-specific) → Modeling → Evaluation.\n",
    "**Team:** Khaled & Adrian (FR document, Binôme B).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Idea** (DL notes, Cap. 9.11): train an autoencoder **only on normal data**. It learns to reconstruct normal road scenes well. On an unexpected object it reconstructs badly, so the **reconstruction error is high** there. The per-pixel error map is the anomaly score, and a threshold turns it into a mask.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two versions in this notebook**\n",
    "- **v1 (sections 2–11):** pixel autoencoder trained from scratch on normal patches; the score is the pixel reconstruction error.\n",
    "- **v2 (sections 12–13):** feature-space autoencoder on frozen VGG16 (ImageNet) features. It is chosen on validation, compared with a no-AE control, and evaluated once on test.\n",
    "- **Final check (sections 14–15):** 11 pretrained backbones and a PaDiM-style density control, compared on validation only. v2 stays the final model, and the test split is not used again.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Decisions inherited from `01_Data_Understanding.ipynb`**\n",
    "\n",
    "| EDA finding | What this notebook does |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| No image is anomaly-free, but about 5,500 64x64 patches of the **train** images are (§9) | Train on anomaly-free **patches** of the train split only |\n",
    "| Working resolution `IMG_SIZE = (352, 640)` (§7) | Same size; the AE is fully convolutional, so it runs on full images at test time |\n",
    "| Objects almost never in the top of the image; no perspective trend (§6) | Augmentation: horizontal flip only |\n",
    "| 9.85 % anomaly pixels, so accuracy is meaningless (§12.1) | No accuracy anywhere |\n",
    "| Score maps: AuPRC is the main metric, AUROC is reported with its chance level (§12.3) | AuPRC, AUROC and AUPRO (FPR cap 0.3) on validation and test |\n",
    "| Several obstacles per image, many of them small (§12.4, §12.7) | Object recall / precision, split into small and large objects |\n",
    "| Speckle under 16 px at full resolution (§12.5) | Objects smaller than 4 px at 352x640 are ignored when counting objects |\n",
    "| Only 9 test images (§12.8) | Test means come with 95 % bootstrap intervals |\n",
    "| Thresholds and model selection on validation only | Test is used **once**, in the last section |"
   ]
  },
