    "## 2. Data preprocessing for the autoencoder\n",
    "The AE must see **normal** content only. Every train image contains an obstacle, so each image is cut into overlapping 64x64 patches and only the patches with **no anomaly pixel** are kept.\n",
    "\n",
    "Annotation borders are not perfectly tight around the objects, so the anomaly mask is first **dilated by a few pixels**. Patches that touch the border of an obstacle are then also discarded.\n",
    "\n",
    "The validation images go through the same steps. Their normal patches give the validation loss used for early stopping (DL notes, Cap. 5.4: never use the test set for that)."
   ]
