    "## 3. Model: convolutional autoencoder\n",
    "Design choices, following the DL notes (Cap. 9):\n",
    "- **Encoder:** convolutions with `stride=2` halve the size four times (64 → 32 → 16 → 8 → 4), as in Lab 7. Hidden layers use **ReLU**; Lab 7 left them linear, which is a bug. The only linear layer is the 2-channel code (see 3.1).\n",
    "- **Bottleneck:** 4x4x2 = 32 values for a 64x64x3 = 12,288-value input. The AE is strongly **undercomplete** (384x compression), so it can only reproduce the *typical* appearance of a road scene, not every local detail. Section 3.1 explains why the bottleneck is this narrow.\n",
    "- **Decoder:** `Conv2DTranspose` with `stride=2` doubles the size back to 64x64. A **sigmoid** output keeps pixels in [0, 1].\n",
    "- **No skip connections:** that would turn it into a U-Net, and the information would bypass the bottleneck (Cap. 10.3).\n",
    "- **Loss:** MSE between the input and its reconstruction. The anomaly score is the same quantity computed per pixel.\n",
    "- **Fully convolutional:** trained on 64x64 patches, it can reconstruct a whole 352x640 image (both sides are divisible by 16)."
   ]
  },
