    "### 3.1 Why such a narrow bottleneck (model selection on validation only)\n",
    "The first version used 3 levels and 16 code channels (12x compression). It reconstructed the obstacles **as well as the road**: boulders, animals and cones came out almost perfect, and the error only lit up on high-contrast textures (stripes, facades, foliage). This is the failure mode of a too-powerful AE described in the DL notes (Cap. 9.6): it \"learns to reconstruct almost anything\".\n",
    "\n",
    "The bottleneck was then narrowed, and the error map was standardised per image (section 5). Every variant was compared on the **validation split only** (9 images, chance AuPRC = 0.091), with the same training recipe:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Encoder levels | Code channels | Compression | Val AuPRC (raw / per-image z) | Val AUROC (raw / per-image z) |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 3 | 16 | 12x | 0.081 / 0.096 | 0.42 / 0.49 |\n",
    "| 3 | 4 | 48x | 0.091 / 0.133 | 0.45 / 0.61 |\n",
    "| 3 | 1 | 192x | 0.089 / 0.101 | 0.46 / 0.55 |\n",
    "| 4 | 8 | 96x | 0.101 / 0.142 | 0.48 / 0.62 |\n",
    "| **4** | **2** | **384x** | **0.113 / 0.151** | **0.54 / 0.67** |\n",
    "\n",
    "(Gaussian smoothing sigma = 8 for all rows.) The search was stopped there on purpose: with 9 validation images, comparing many more variants would start to fit the validation set itself.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Seed check: ReLU vs linear code.** With only 2 code channels, a ReLU bottleneck can collapse if a unit dies (DL notes, Cap. 4.3.1). Each version was trained with 3 seeds (validation only, sigma = 16):\n",
    "\n",
    "| Code activation | Val MSE (mean ± std) | Val AuPRC | Val AUROC | Note |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| ReLU | 0.0084 ± 0.0019 | 0.137 ± 0.016 | 0.655 ± 0.030 | one seed collapsed (val MSE 0.011) |\n",
    "| **Linear** | **0.0069 ± 0.0000** | **0.150 ± 0.002** | **0.680 ± 0.004** | stable |\n",
    "\n",
    "The linear code is kept. Its results barely depend on the seed, so the single-seed numbers below are representative.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Transparency note:** the test split was evaluated once with the first version, as part of the same notebook run, before this change. The change was decided on the validation numbers above only."
   ]
  },
