   "source": [
    "## 12. v2: a feature-space autoencoder (validation only)\n",
    "Section 11 showed the limit of the pixel autoencoder: pixel error measures *unusual colour and texture*, not *unexpected object*. Grey boulders on a grey road are missed and foliage is flagged.\n",
    "\n",
    "v2 keeps the autoencoder idea but moves it to a better space. A network pretrained on ImageNet (VGG16, **frozen**, used only as a fixed measuring tool) turns each image region into a feature vector. The autoencoder learns to reconstruct the feature vectors of **normal road scenes**, and an obstacle is a region whose features it cannot reconstruct.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rules for this section (same protocol as before):\n",
    "- every choice uses the **validation split only**; the train masks are used only to learn the road prior (12.6);\n",
    "- the list of candidates is **short on purpose**: with 9 validation images, trying many variants would fit the validation set itself;\n",
    "- a component is kept only if it raises the validation AuPRC by more than the **seed noise of section 3.1 (0.002)**;\n",
    "- the **test split is used once**, at the end (12.8)."
   ]
  },
