    "### 12.2 Control experiment: where does the gain come from?\n",
    "The simplest use of VGG is a **perceptual error**: compare the VGG features of the image with those of the pixel autoencoder's reconstruction (first idea of the v1 next steps, section 14). Before trusting it, it must be compared with a **control that uses no reconstruction at all**: the size (L2 norm) of the feature vector at each position. If both score the same, the gain comes from the pretrained network and not from the autoencoder, and calling it \"the autoencoder's result\" would be wrong."
