   "source": [
    "**Reading the control.** The perceptual error is far better than the pixel MSE, but the control without any reconstruction scores **the same** at every depth. The improvement comes from the ImageNet features (an obstacle simply activates VGG more strongly than asphalt), not from the pixel autoencoder. The perceptual error of the v1 model is therefore **not** used.\n",
    "\n",
    "The autoencoder has to work **in feature space** to contribute: it must learn what the features of a normal road look like. From here on, every result of the feature autoencoder is shown next to the same control, so its own contribution stays visible."
   ]
