   "source": [
    "### 12.3 Preprocessing for the feature autoencoder\n",
    "- **Normal cells.** The AE is trained only on normal data (DL notes, Cap. 9). A feature cell counts as normal if its image region contains no anomaly pixel, after dilating each obstacle by `FEATURE_MARGIN` px (same idea as the normal patches of section 2). The training input is the whole feature map, and the anomaly cells get **weight 0 in the loss**.\n",
    "- **Standardisation.** VGG channels have very different scales, so each channel is z-scored with the mean and standard deviation of the **train** normal cells (the usual input scaling, fitted on train only)."
   ]
  },
