   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d266939",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12.4 Model: autoencoder on feature maps\n",
    "The same design rules as v1, adapted to features:\n",
    "- **no stride**: a feature cell already summarises a whole image region, so the AE compresses the channels of each cell (with a 3x3 neighbourhood) instead of the image size;\n",
    "- **narrow linear code** (8 channels per cell), for the same reasons as section 3.1: a wide code would also reconstruct the obstacles, and a 2-to-8-channel ReLU code can die;\n",
    "- **linear output**: standardised features can be negative and unbounded, so a sigmoid would cut them;\n",
    "- **masked MSE**: anomaly cells get weight 0, so the AE only ever learns normal road features;\n",
    "- **early stopping on the validation normal cells**, never on test."
   ]
  },
