   "source": [
    "## 15. Final results for Binôme B\n",
    "\n",
    "**Final model: v2, unchanged.** It is the feature autoencoder on frozen VGG16 `block5_conv3` features (section 12). On validation, none of the 10 other pretrained backbones gives a better feature AE, so the decision rule of section 14 keeps v2 and **the test split was not used again**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Test results of the final model** (from 12.8; every choice was made on validation):\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Test | 95 % CI | Chance / reference |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| AuPRC (main) | **0.631** | — | prevalence 0.086 |\n",
    "| AUROC | 0.922 | — | 0.5 |\n",
    "| AUPRO @ FPR 0.3 | 0.823 | — | 0.15 |\n",
    "| Pixel F1 = Dice, per-image mean | 0.623 | 0.506 – 0.729 | v1: 0.245 |\n",
    "| Pixel IoU, per-image mean | 0.474 | 0.355 – 0.583 | v1: 0.158 |\n",
    "| Object recall / false alarms | 16/22 objects, 10 of 22 predicted blobs | — | v1: 16/22, 36 of 42 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Overall backbone comparison (validation, feature AE, 14.3).** Speed is the feature extraction on the RTX 4060 at 352x640; parameters count the backbone up to the layer used.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Rank | Backbone | AE AuPRC | AE AUROC | AE AUPRO | Best control AuPRC | AE − control | Params (M) | ms / image |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 1 | **VGG16** | **0.596** | 0.913 | 0.700 | 0.629 | −0.033 | 14.7 | 24.4 |\n",
    "| 2 | VGG19 | 0.592 | 0.924 | 0.655 | 0.604 | −0.012 | 20.0 | 30.1 |\n",
    "| 3 | Xception | 0.588 | 0.928 | **0.788** | 0.587 | +0.001 | 14.1 | 22.1 |\n",
    "| 4 | ResNet50 | 0.541 | 0.927 | 0.730 | 0.523 | +0.018 | 8.6 | 26.3 |\n",
    "| 5 | DenseNet121 | 0.527 | 0.918 | 0.748 | 0.513 | +0.014 | 4.3 | 32.9 |\n",
    "| 6 | ResNet101 | 0.509 | 0.906 | 0.733 | 0.496 | +0.013 | 27.7 | 44.1 |\n",
    "| 7 | EfficientNetV2S | 0.465 | 0.908 | 0.710 | 0.447 | +0.018 | 5.3 | 27.0 |\n",
    "| 8 | ConvNeXtTiny | 0.381 | 0.850 | 0.610 | 0.448 | −0.067 | 12.3 | 26.8 |\n",
    "| 9 | EfficientNetB0 | 0.378 | 0.878 | 0.596 | 0.358 | +0.020 | 0.9 | 19.1 |\n",
    "| 10 | MobileNetV3Large | 0.347 | 0.851 | 0.559 | 0.354 | −0.007 | 0.8 | 15.3 |\n",
    "| 11 | ResNet50V2 | 0.310 | 0.833 | 0.532 | 0.322 | −0.012 | 7.5 | 21.1 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reading the comparison**\n",
    "- **The best overall is VGG16**, with VGG19 and Xception just behind. The three differ by less than 0.01 AuPRC, which is within the noise of 9 validation images. Xception has the best region-level score (AUPRO 0.788 vs 0.700) and is slightly faster, so it is a reasonable alternative if region coverage matters more than pixel precision. It was not sent to test, because the decision rule uses the main metric only.\n",
    "- **Newer ImageNet backbones are not better here.** ResNet, EfficientNet, MobileNet and ConvNeXt score 0.31 – 0.54, although they are stronger classifiers. A likely reason (a hypothesis, not tested here): VGG has no batch normalisation and no residual shortcuts, so the *size* of its activations still says \"there is a salient object here\". The feature norm alone reaches 0.63 on VGG16 but only 0.27 – 0.49 on the batch-normalised networks. The newer networks are trained to be more invariant, which helps classification but removes part of that signal.\n",
    "- **AE vs density model.** The feature AE beats the best density control on 6 of the 11 backbones, by +0.013 to +0.020 AuPRC, and loses on the others. On the two best backbones (VGG16 and VGG19) it loses to the simple feature norm. Overall, **with 42 training images the autoencoder does about as well as a Gaussian fitted on the same features**. Most of the detection ability comes from the pretrained representation. This is the main scientific conclusion of Binôme B.\n",
    "- **Speed is not a constraint.** Every backbone runs in 15 – 44 ms per image on the RTX 4060, so the choice can be made on quality alone. VGG16 inference also fits the 6 GB RTX 2060.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Test usage, in total:** three evaluations (v1 with a ReLU code, v1 with a linear code, v2). Sections 14 – 15 did not use the test split.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitations** (detailed in section 13): small objects (validation small-object recall 4/12), coarse 16-px boundaries, labelled-only anomalies vs other objects (bollards, pedestrians), very small evaluation sets, and ImageNet pre-training as external knowledge (to be stated in the report and confirmed as allowed for Binôme B)."
